<!--
  BlockML Core — type reference marker for aggregation payloads

  FQN: org.blockml.bml.core.TypeReference
-->
<block
  xmlns="http://blockml.org/schema/block"
  xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
  xsi:schemaLocation="http://blockml.org/schema/block https://blockml.org/schemas/core/block.xsd
                      "
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:bml="http://blockml.org/schema/bml">

  <idea>Marks an aggregation whose children are Block type references, not Block instances.</idea>

  <documentation>Abstract generic marker for aggregation payloads that list Block types by direct
    element reference — the child element name resolves to an FQN via xmlns prefix. Analogous to
    org.blockml.bml.core.PrimitiveEntity(T) for primitive values in composition: TypeReference(T)
    is never instantiated directly; children reference T, not TypeReference itself.

    Use on aggregation type attributes to distinguish type-reference collections from instance
    collections:
    • core:TypeReference(core:Block)[]     — contracts, subTypes, Library _blocks
    • core:TypeReference(core:Block)[1..1] — type, baseType identity on Block definitions
    • core:TypeReference(core:Language)[]  — languages
    • core:TypeReference(core:Capability)[] — when listing capability types only

    Validator detection: aggregation type is a generic application of org.blockml.bml.core.TypeReference
    with exactly one type argument T. Each child element name must resolve to an FQN that satisfies
    satisfiesTypeBound(fqn, T). Forbidden on TypeReference aggregations: member values on children,
    bml:id, bml:version (except where a specific aggregation documents an exception), nested
    composition, and default="true".

    Contrast with org.blockml.bml.type.FullyQualifiedName(B) — a ValueType for a single scalar FQN
    on Property type attributes. TypeReference(T) describes the XML container pattern where the
    referenced type appears as the child element name.

    Optional concrete aliases (for example BlockReference = TypeReference(core:Block)) may bind T
    via baseType for shorter authoring — not required in V1.</documentation>

  <references>
    <see file="17_type_system_bml.md">
      TypeReference marker, validator rules, and contrast with FullyQualifiedName.
    </see>
    <see file="16_framework_base_types.md">
      contracts, subTypes, languages container pattern.
    </see>
    <see block="core:PrimitiveEntity">
      Inverse pattern — wraps primitive values as Entity instances in composition.
    </see>
    <see block="def:BlockDefinition">
      type, baseType, contracts, languages, subTypes aggregations.
    </see>
    <see block="def:AggregationDefinition">
      Member aggregation type attribute — TypeReference(T) vs plain Block[].
    </see>
    <see block="btype:FullyQualifiedName">
      Scalar FQN ValueType — not a type-reference container.
    </see>
  </references>

  <name>TypeReference</name>
  <type>
    <core:TypeReference />
  </type>
  <baseType>
    <core:Entity />
  </baseType>
  <abstract>true</abstract>

  <genericTypes>
    <T baseType="core:Block">
      <documentation>Block branch constraint for child element references. Each child element name
        must resolve to an FQN that satisfies satisfiesTypeBound(fqn, T).</documentation>
    </T>
  </genericTypes>

</block>
